{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~","id":101263,"title":"~ Lunar Fashion Sense in Third Edition ~","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-29T07:59:02-07:00","id":101263,"title":"~ Lunar Fashion Sense in Third Edition ~","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i2.minus.com/jtUO8VZak2mMU.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <hr /><br /> Behold! A handsome weretiger in a classy red hanbok! Now now, while I know that the writer has stated there will be Lunars who come from the city, I still worry about the majority of artwork will still feature Roid-Rage Monster in Loincloth and Bikini that plagued the MoEP:Lunars book.<br /> <br /> I understand that not every Lunars has moonsilver clothing so it's more logical to wear as little as possible so you don't have to waste money buying new shirt everytime you shapeshift, but seeing a Lunar wearing stereotype barbarian costume just make me roll my eyes and think &quot;Lunar: the Werewolf&quot; every time.<br /> <br /> So I guess that it'll be great if we see more Lunar who dress in Resource 5 cloth in Ex3 and less seashell-bra No Moon or shirtless + fur-skirt combo Full Moon.<br /> <br /> And I'm out before this turn into a DB's imperialism or Lunar theme thread again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:12:07-07:00","id":101267,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm pretty happy to have the barbarian aesthetic back, because I like barbarians and think 2nd ed had too much City-States and not enough cool barbarian tribes and cultures. I can see that there might be a worry that 3rd ed Barbarians will be back to bad old &quot;cities bad! Raiding good!&quot; 1st ed Lunars.<br /> But actually, of all the Lunars I've seen played, I don't remember any that were really much into the barbarian aesthetic, in practice. One No Moon mongol... but he reads books and wears egyptian clothes, so... Others have included an Immaculate Monk, a girl from Nexus, and a committed member of the Cult of the Illuminated. 3 out of 4 of them weren't even cannibals! What sort of Lunars don't even rip out people's still-beating hearts as a sacrifice to their dark Goddess and consume it?<br /> <br /> But saying that: Barbarian doesn't have to mean bikinis and furry jockstraps. Honestly, it shouldn't, few barbarian cultures ever actually wore that kind of thing.<br /> A wide variety of fur-based or other primitive clothing would be fine with me.<br /> Actually, I'd rather see Lunars flat-out naked than wearing silly furry bikinis (I imagine their genitals would have to be blocked by strategic object placement, but whatever, I'm looking for realistic costumes, not porn). If you spend a lot of time in animal form, thinking like an animal, and you're worried about breaking clothes by mutating, well for the more barbaric Lunars why even bother with clothes? A lot of barbarian cultures in the real world had a fairly lax attitude towards wearing clothes (actually, it's more that cultures with a lax attitude to clothes tended to be considered to be barbarians, since barbarian is essentially a pejorative label).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:41:27-07:00","id":101291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~#post101263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that not every Lunars has moonsilver clothing so it's more logical to wear as little as possible so you don't have to waste money buying new shirt everytime you shapeshift, but seeing a Lunar wearing stereotype barbarian costume just make me roll my eyes and think &quot;Lunar: the Werewolf&quot; every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Plumage Mastery. Never buy clothes. At least if your ST says you don't have to.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I hate the barbarian look. My Lunars almost always come from the city. The only character I'm playing at the moment (games are sparse, hence my forum activity) is a Tepet. The one before that was from Great Forks. Screw loincloths. Either wear something nice or don't wear anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:45:14-07:00","id":101293,"title":"","content":"Two words: cargo shorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:51:14-07:00","id":101300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101267#post101267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But saying that: Barbarian doesn't have to mean bikinis and furry jockstraps. Honestly, it shouldn't, few barbarian cultures ever actually wore that kind of thing.<br /> A wide variety of fur-based or other primitive clothing would be fine with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but why restrict yourself? Your clothing can be anything. I'm as big a fan of Robert E. Howard as anyone, but why stick with the Viking / Mongol / Zulu aesthetic when you can reflexively adapt to be a paragon of fashion according to whatever culture you find yourself in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I'd rather see Lunars flat-out naked than wearing silly furry bikinis (I imagine their genitals would have to be blocked by strategic object placement, but whatever, I'm looking for realistic costumes, not porn). If you spend a lot of time in animal form, thinking like an animal, and you're worried about breaking clothes by mutating, well for the more barbaric Lunars why even bother with clothes? A lot of barbarian cultures in the real world had a fairly lax attitude towards wearing clothes (actually, it's more that cultures with a lax attitude to clothes tended to be considered to be barbarians, since barbarian is essentially a pejorative label). </div> </div> </div>Naked is good. And there doesn't even need to be any genitals showing. Depending on your weirdness level, you've probably got a gleaming silver carapace or you're made of fire or you just choose not to have reproductive parts when you're not planning to use them. No one complains about animals and elementals and demons going around uncovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:06:30-07:00","id":101306,"title":"","content":"If you have a coherent aesthetics of loincloth barbarians, the contrast of having a few pictures with different aesthetics makes them that much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:41:49-07:00","id":101337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101293#post101293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two words: cargo shorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>TDO has joined the heretical Shorts Faction, deviating from the one true path of the Winding Pants Faction! What does this say about the future of Lunars!?!<br /> <br /> More seriously, I'd bet there will be lots of clothing variety amongst the Lunars in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:59:06-07:00","id":101378,"title":"","content":"I can stomach the cargo shorts as long as they're not wearing shirts with popped collars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1225-naz","name":"Naz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1225_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:20:33-07:00","id":101394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Naz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101378#post101378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can stomach the cargo shorts as long as they're not wearing shirts with popped collars.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that would be a reason enough for Dragon Blooded to hunt them unto the edge of the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-29-2014, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:46:02-07:00","id":101401,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of generic &quot;barbarian clothing&quot; either. It's dumb and stereotypical, and seems ill-suited for a splat that is likely going to change its appearance as part of its social tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:03:01-07:00","id":101405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101267#post101267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm pretty happy to have the barbarian aesthetic back, because I like barbarians and think 2nd ed had too much City-States and not enough cool barbarian tribes and cultures. I can see that there might be a worry that 3rd ed Barbarians will be back to bad old &quot;cities bad! Raiding good!&quot; 1st ed Lunars.<br /> But actually, of all the Lunars I've seen played, I don't remember any that were really much into the barbarian aesthetic, in practice. One No Moon mongol... but he reads books and wears egyptian clothes, so... Others have included an Immaculate Monk, a girl from Nexus, and a committed member of the Cult of the Illuminated. 3 out of 4 of them weren't even cannibals! What sort of Lunars don't even rip out people's still-beating hearts as a sacrifice to their dark Goddess and consume it?<br /> <br /> But saying that: Barbarian doesn't have to mean bikinis and furry jockstraps. Honestly, it shouldn't, few barbarian cultures ever actually wore that kind of thing.<br /> A wide variety of fur-based or other primitive clothing would be fine with me.<br /> Actually, I'd rather see Lunars flat-out naked than wearing silly furry bikinis (I imagine their genitals would have to be blocked by strategic object placement, but whatever, I'm looking for realistic costumes, not porn). If you spend a lot of time in animal form, thinking like an animal, and you're worried about breaking clothes by mutating, well for the more barbaric Lunars why even bother with clothes? A lot of barbarian cultures in the real world had a fairly lax attitude towards wearing clothes (actually, it's more that cultures with a lax attitude to clothes tended to be considered to be barbarians, since barbarian is essentially a pejorative label).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that barbarian aesthetic is bad, I'm saying that &quot;generic barbarian&quot; aesthetic that keep popping up in Second Edition artwork (sometime in fluff too, just look at all the FA Lunars) is bad, and Lunar Exaltation only choosing barbarian as its host is bad too.<br /> <br /> And I do hope the comment about naked Lunar is sarcasm because I don't want to smash my laptop whenever somebody look at the screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:08:17-07:00","id":101410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101405#post101405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying that barbarian aesthetic is bad, I'm saying that &quot;generic barbarian&quot; aesthetic that keep popping up in Second Edition artwork (sometime in fluff too, just look at all the FA Lunars) is bad, and Lunar Exaltation only choosing barbarian as its host is bad too.<br /> <br /> And I do hope the comment about naked Lunar is sarcasm because I don't want to smash my laptop whenever somebody look at the screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't. Nudity is a thing, and depending on how inhuman the Lunar becomes, they may forego anything that reminds them of humanity. All possibilities should be on the table and I strongly believe nudity can be done tastefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:21:48-07:00","id":101419,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Lunar and clothes I think of Morena of Keychain. She wore a variety of dresses and outfit depending on what was regionally appropriate and when she shape shifted they went to elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:00:34-07:00","id":101436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Naz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101378#post101378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can stomach the cargo shorts as long as they're not wearing shirts with popped collars.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the Liminal Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:02:27-07:00","id":101438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101436#post101436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's the Liminal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I have come back from realms of unimaginable horror. <i>Fashion</i> horror.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:13:06-07:00","id":101448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101438#post101438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I have come back from realms of unimaginable horror. <i>Fashion</i> horror.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I was thinking, &quot;They call me a mass murderer, a monster, a terrorist. I'm all of these things.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-29-2014, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T14:07:08-07:00","id":101489,"title":"","content":"Rather than evincing a single, barbarian aesthetic, I believe Lunars should wear garments that blend personal tastes with the constraints of their physical and cultural environments. Some elders may go sans clothing, but speaking from an anthropological view, clothing has a variety of purposes, not the least of which is insulating the body in climates that are not tropical.<br /> <br /> There are a number of fashions seen as barbaric by historical peoples, usually related to association with cultural otherness or violation of that people's cultural norms. These can vary in the extreme, encompassing everything from fur robes, sarongs and body wraps, or even trousers depending on the culture in question. Since all of these are barbaric from a certain perspective, we need to consider both which perspectives are dominant (likely the Realm / major cities) and what elements they might find alien or barbarous.<br /> <br /> In short, while any Exalt can wear whatever clothing fits their personal expression, the barbarian aesthetic should make sense within the constraints of culture and climate. YMMV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/734-zombie_eyes","name":"Zombie_Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T18:52:27-07:00","id":101663,"title":"","content":"I was going to pull something from <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/search?q=dog+outfits&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=43c3U9uIHaem2gXhgoGABQ&amp;ved=0CAgQ_AUoAQ&amp;biw=1920&amp;bih=879\" target=\"_blank\">this google search</a> but really it's all so good that I can't choose.<br /> <br /> Barbarian aesthetic is OK so long as it's not presented as a Lunar monoculture, but I really hope 3e manages to avoid the &quot;Lunars are brown people&quot; trope this time round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:10:09-07:00","id":101670,"title":"","content":"It's amazing dogs haven't just murdered us all in our sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:52:45-07:00","id":101698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~#post101263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that not every Lunars has moonsilver clothing so it's more logical to wear as little as possible so you don't have to waste money buying new shirt everytime you shapeshift</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you intend not to mingle with non-barbarian cultures of Creation.<br /> It seems that a lot of this attitute is a remnant of the &quot;barbarian lunar&quot; stereotype of the 1st edition. You can't wear pants and a nice shirt, or Luna will come and take your Exaltation away. Besides, why would you ever think about living in a city? Go into the wild, to breed your beastmen army and burn that city down! That's the only way to be sure that such weakening thoughts will never come back to you again.<br /> <br /> Lunars come from many cultures of the Creation. Therefore they should have their own preferences towards clothing. Unless something really drastic happened to them (Ma Ha Suchi, i am looking at you), someone that was fashion-conscious before Exaltation is unlikely to start wearing loincloths just because.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:22:33-07:00","id":101784,"title":"","content":"I wasn't joking about naked Lunars. I'd much prefer flat-out naked Lunars to ones who wear revealing clothing (as per most fantasy art). And I'd also like to see practical clothing.<br /> <br /> But it was a good point about Changing Plumage Mastery. My Lunar PC never buys clothes, just changes his clothes to fit the occasion and culture he's in.<br /> I'd certainly be happy to see art showing the same Lunar having them in several different costumes, to fit in with whatever culture they're in. Some barbarian, some civilised, etc.<br /> <br /> I should also say... I'm glad to see a barbarian aesthetic for Lunars, not because I want Lunars particularly to be barbarians, but because I like barbarians.<br /> I'd be very happy to see Solar artwork showing a whole bunch of Solars in furs, or whatever.<br /> <br /> (But not loincloths. Ridiculously muscled viking-esque man in furry loincloth might be the stereotypical look for a barbarian, but loincloths aren't really a thing in any barbarian cultures where it's not ridiculously hot, because you'll freeze to death. Sensible barbarian aesthetics, please.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T07:09:57-07:00","id":101905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101784#post101784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't joking about naked Lunars. I'd much prefer flat-out naked Lunars to ones who wear revealing clothing (as per most fantasy art).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I would like this kind of in general as well. It's not as if nudity is titillating in all contexts and cultures.<br /> <br /> Maybe also a measure of detachment from the idea that comparative cultural sophistication necessarily equates to how many clothes you wear; ancient Egyptians basically all wore loincloths and simple kilts, and were otherwise topless (social status conveyed by how elaborately dyed your clothing was and how much jewellery and cosmetics you had).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should also say... I'm glad to see a barbarian aesthetic for Lunars, not because I want Lunars particularly to be barbarians, but because I like barbarians.<br /> I'd be very happy to see Solar artwork showing a whole bunch of Solars in furs, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.scoilnet.ie/womeninhistory/content/unit2/wildirish.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Yeeeessss...</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(But not loincloths. Ridiculously muscled viking-esque man in furry loincloth might be the stereotypical look for a barbarian, but loincloths aren't really a thing in any barbarian cultures where it's not ridiculously hot, because you'll freeze to death. Sensible barbarian aesthetics, please.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an idea for a Lunar character from the far North who wears an old Shogunate dress uniform; it's kind of a statement of ownership of the manse where she found it, and also contrasts with her environment without it needing to be about exposure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:17:48-07:00","id":102014,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/GBs0zwx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2031-savior-girl","name":"Savior Girl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2031_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:39:30-07:00","id":102022,"title":"","content":"There shall be no fashion among the chosen of Luna! Fashion is for those weak-bellied city dwellers who desire shortbread and toilet paper! The silver host shall crush the weak, cowering, fashionable civilizations beneath-<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I'm not sure what came over me there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:05:37-07:00","id":102043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=102022#post102022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There shall be no fashion among the chosen of Luna! Fashion is for those weak-bellied city dwellers who desire shortbread and toilet paper! The silver host shall crush the weak, cowering, fashionable civilizations beneath-<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I'm not sure what came over me there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called <i>lunacy</i>. Something that apparently Lunars don't have a lot to do with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:18:02-07:00","id":102049,"title":"","content":"This thread prompted me to look up various &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures from around the world (Aztecs, Tlingit, Mongols, Bedouins, the Norse, et cetera), and then did the same for the <i>word</i> barbarian.<br /> <br /> Turns out the latter has basically nothing to do with the former, visually, except when the barbarians were shirtless vikings. Mostly, they were more like gladiators, which I guess is what you get when the trendsetter was a swords and sandals movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:22:52-07:00","id":102054,"title":"","content":"Okay, see, here's my thing.<br /> <br /> Why does the Silver Exaltation pick you? I need to know that before I make any call on what kind of people Lunars will generally be. 2nd edition, it was <b>survival</b>, so yeah, being a wilderness born <i>savage</i> that got in some deep shit but came out in tact, I can see that.<br /> <br /> I could also see a city street rat who stepped into enemy gang territory, a peasant villager who went to cut wood and found himself up to his eyeballs in bandits or even a noble man who found himself bereft of his luxuries and surrounded by those who wanted to bereft him of his life.<br /> <br /> Now since the Silver Exaltation wouldn't alter their minds, they don't have reasons to go naked or wear furs.<br /> <br /> I dunno what 3e Moon Shards will be looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:51:45-07:00","id":102077,"title":"","content":"Cargo shorts. Muddy, well-worn cargo shorts. With sturdy sandals and a sleeveless forest-camo tunic type thing, and a leather cord necklace with little seedpods and bones on it. (The Hunters in Darkness illustration in the Werewolf corebook comes to mind for some reason.)<br /> Or cargo shorts and a shirt made out of beer can tabs, with shoes made out of rubber chickens. Who knows? It's possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ashes to embers<br /> Dust to flame<br /> A phoenix takes flight<br /> Forever has changed","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2395-stygian-ash","name":"Stygian Ash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:56:38-07:00","id":102329,"title":"","content":"Nothing about being a Lunar says you can't dress nicely.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.anime-planet.com/images/characters/crocodile_gentleman_57675.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T20:03:54-07:00","id":102335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=102054#post102054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the Silver Exaltation pick you? I need to know that before I make any call on what kind of people Lunars will generally be. 2nd edition, it was <b>survival</b>, so yeah, being a wilderness born <i>savage</i> that got in some deep shit but came out in tact, I can see that.<br /> <br /> I dunno what 3e Moon Shards will be looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly cargo shorts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T20:19:36-07:00","id":102342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=101784#post101784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't joking about naked Lunars. I'd much prefer flat-out naked Lunars to ones who wear revealing clothing (as per most fantasy art). And I'd also like to see practical clothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call forth Unlimited Full Frontal Assault Works! I'm literally the bone of my sword!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:43:08-07:00","id":102650,"title":"","content":"Just sayin', Conan wore dozens of different outfits in his stories; just about the only times he was in just a loincloth was when he literally crawled through the mud for days on end to assassinate this really bastardly fellow, or had swam for a few days to escape being murdered by pirates and then dragged himself up onto a ship. More often he at least had some breeks and usually *some* armor. He certainly wasn't buck-naked when sitting the throne of Aquilonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:52:59-07:00","id":102658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=102650#post102650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just sayin', Conan wore dozens of different outfits in his stories; just about the only times he was in just a loincloth was when he literally crawled through the mud for days on end to assassinate this really bastardly fellow, or had swam for a few days to escape being murdered by pirates and then dragged himself up onto a ship. More often he at least had some breeks and usually *some* armor. He certainly wasn't buck-naked when sitting the throne of Aquilonia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never read the book, but a Google search sure make me think Cona the Barbarian = Stereotype shirtless Barbarian with loincloth and fur-skirt guy.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.minus.com/jsxlmVxyOnhgP.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:55:28-07:00","id":102661,"title":"","content":"Your Windows theme. Ermahgerd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:57:03-07:00","id":102664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=102661#post102661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Windows theme. Ermahgerd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take that as a compliment then &gt;;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:57:30-07:00","id":102665,"title":"","content":"That was actually what set Conan apart as a character - he wasn't actually stereotype. Clothing aside, he was always rather brooding and contemplative and philosophical. Also violent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:59:15-07:00","id":102668,"title":"","content":"The movies were hardly very faithful to the books - one thing that immediately jumps to the forefront is that <i>literally every Conan story Howard wrote</i> described Conan as having black hair and blue eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not saying Conan wouldn't ever be in just a loincloth - it's more that for every time when that was the case, there were three instances of him bashing in someone's skull with a beef-bone. :P<br /> <br /> That said, I'm starting to think that a statted-out Conan needs a Melee specialty of &quot;Food.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:24:41-07:00","id":102695,"title":"","content":"A google images search of &quot;Conan&quot; and &quot;frazetta&quot; gets much the same imagery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:38:01-07:00","id":102711,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: Frank Frazetta almost never <i>read </i>the stuff he did cover illustrations for, and was in fact known for drawing more or less whatever the hell he felt like, regardless of what the commissioner had asked for. It really speaks to the man's talent that he kept getting hired anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:43:21-07:00","id":102715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/101263-~-lunar-fashion-sense-in-third-edition-~?p=102711#post102711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: Frank Frazetta almost never <i>read </i>the stuff he did cover illustrations for, and was in fact known for drawing more or less whatever the hell he felt like, regardless of what the commissioner had asked for. It really speaks to the man's talent that he kept getting hired anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is pretty common, actually. I'm not sure how much you'd have to pay to get an illustrator who was high quality <i>and </i>high fidelity, but it'd be a scary amount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:46:53-07:00","id":102719,"title":"","content":"Not disputing that the images are not in sync with the stories. But if people go looking for images that are &quot;Conan like&quot; or &quot;barbarians&quot; --actual pictures, not word images-- scowls, bare chests and loincloths are going to be most of what they find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:55:00-07:00","id":102875,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Conan,&quot; Natala ventured finally, &quot;when you fought the monster, and later, as you came up the corridor, did you see anything of\u2014of Thalis?&quot;</i><br /> <i>He shook his head. &quot;It was dark in the corridor; but it was empty.&quot;</i><br /> <i>She shuddered. &quot;She tortured me\u2014yet I pity her.&quot;</i><br /> <i>&quot;It was a hot welcome we got in that accursed city,&quot; he snarled. Then his grim humor returned. &quot;Well, they'll remember our visit long enough, I'll wager. There are brains and guts and blood to be cleaned off the marble tiles, and if their god still lives, he carries more wounds than I. We got off light, after all: we have wine and water and a good chance of reaching a habitable country, though I look as if I've gone through a meatgrinder, and you have a sore\u2014&quot;</i><br /> <i>&quot;It's all your fault,&quot; she interrupted. &quot;If you had not looked so long and admiringly at that Stygian cat\u2014&quot;</i><br /> <i>&quot;Crom and his devils!&quot; he swore. &quot;When the oceans drown the world, women will take time for jealousy. Devil take their conceit! Did I tell the Stygian to fall in love with me? After all, she was only human!&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}